                                        "entry_id": "fc50b186-3931-32d4-a2a6-9d86af56ab51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any traditional theatrical work, combining drama, music, song and sometimes dance.",
                                            "Traditional Chinese opera, performed outdoors. The equivalent term in Mandarin is 街戲 /街戏 (jiēxì, literally “street opera”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Malaysia",
                                            "Singapore",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f870def9-96d6-36a2-a0b1-ff2976ff2762",
                                        "entry_id": "fc50b186-3931-32d4-a2a6-9d86af56ab51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Insincere behaviour; an act meant to deceive or mislead."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Singapore",
                                            "Singlish",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9adc47fe-43c1-4fc5-b2cb-a2e842d68c6c",
                                                "sense_id": "f870def9-96d6-36a2-a0b1-ff2976ff2762",
                                                "text": "They have to review whether they have revealed too much to the public before the wayang goes on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50ec81d6-8d90-4949-a822-5a2c61947e9d",
                                                "sense_id": "f870def9-96d6-36a2-a0b1-ff2976ff2762",
                                                "text": "There had been two important reservations made on the practice of consultation and consensus. […] The other reservation is that consultation and consensus is no more than a “wayang”, because views are not accepted and no changes are made to the original policy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecd9173c-6373-4fe6-823e-b46dd305b32e",
                                                "sense_id": "f870def9-96d6-36a2-a0b1-ff2976ff2762",
                                                "text": "Besides being adept at directing actors from behind the camera, [Royston] Tan is a bit of a wayang king himself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4623e6c5-281e-44d1-8030-cf9691e105d0",
                                                "sense_id": "f870def9-96d6-36a2-a0b1-ff2976ff2762",
                                                "text": "Dr Chee called the polls a ‘wayang’ and said they were being held so that the PAP could claim to have the people’s mandate to govern."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74251d76-e7f5-4a15-9f05-d28aacc84a5d",
                                                "sense_id": "f870def9-96d6-36a2-a0b1-ff2976ff2762",
                                                "text": "Mr [Inderjit] Singh […] had said earlier that Mr [James] Gomez told him the minority certificate incident was just a ‘wayang’, Malay for theatre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wayang",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c79d1aa5-753d-3644-af0e-8f5f70d3c6b3",
                                        "entry_id": "830737d1-4fe6-34c8-a544-9166689a7fd2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put up a front, to pretend (e.g., to be hard at work when one’s superiors are watching) or behave in a false and misleading way, especially if it puts one at an advantage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Singapore",
                                            "Singlish",
                                            "invariable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d724faa-2c2f-4e81-943d-43baec2001a3",
                                                "sense_id": "c79d1aa5-753d-3644-af0e-8f5f70d3c6b3",
                                                "text": "[…] some [MPs] have to do wayang wayang in the evening like meet the people sessions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1e1bf30-e5b7-4bf9-a8c2-79c167b24bae",
                                                "sense_id": "c79d1aa5-753d-3644-af0e-8f5f70d3c6b3",
                                                "text": "It’s taboo to say that you’re free, even if you have nothing to do, because that’s like asking to get fired. I think it’s obvious whether someone’s actually busy or just wayang-ing—they start toggling between the same documents or surreptitiously using their phone—we just don’t talk about it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
